  "problem": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/94dfa3a04ebb45507d09ae557079c4f165c63ac6fa58f7c977ee152441b9e1bd.png)\n\nUse the model above to find the value of $\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}.$",
  "worked_solution": "![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/linear/14153326/assets/a60284df5200b84835d261462207e386d975bd4757608919928cabf68623e5fd.png)\n\nWe can break down our division problem as follows:\n\n- Computing $\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}$ means we want to determine how many times $\\frac{5}{6}$ fits into $\\frac{2}{6}.$\n\n- Since both fractions have a *common denominator*, this is the *same* as determining how many times $5$ fits into $2.$\n\n- Therefore, instead of $\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}$, we can simply compute $2÷5.$\n\nSo, we have\n\n$$\n2÷5=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$\n\nTherefore, we conclude that\n\n$$\n\\frac{2}{6}÷\\frac{5}{6}=\\frac{2}{5}.\n$$",
